    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1355">

                <pb facs="1219" n="961" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg961"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>446. Your 459, February 28, does not clearly indicate what message German
                    Ambassador desires you to communicate to commander Allied fleet, but it would
                    appear that message you are requested to <pb facs="1220" n="962" xml:id="pg962"
                    /> communicate might more properly be given by Turkish military commander. If,
                    however, it is proposed to evacuate Constantinople, you may, if requested, act
                    as intermediary to save city from bombardment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
